#!/bin/sh
# UserPromptSubmit hook: remind the agent of the conversation-tracking rule on every prompt.
# Never blocks; prints the reminder as additionalContext. Procedure: .claude/issue-tracker.md.
# This repo is public: tracking lives in a private Linear project, never in GitHub issues or repo files.
cat <<'JSON'
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"UserPromptSubmit","additionalContext":"threejs-worldgen tracking rule: if this prompt reports a bug, proposes a feature or design idea, states a rule/invariant, or you discover a bug while working, file it or update its existing issue IN THIS SAME REPLY in the private Linear project `threejs-worldgen` (team Askalice, key ASK) — NOT GitHub issues: this repo is public. Search first (list_issues with query) and update instead of duplicating. Body = current summary with the user's words quoted verbatim under Reported, plus cause/decisions/repro/acceptance criteria; add a dated comment for new detail. Place it in the hierarchy (project milestone -> Epic -> Story -> Task, children via parentId; labels Epic/Story/Task plus Feature/Bug/Improvement/Documentation); label ready-for-agent when fully specified, needs-info when cause or design is open. Never copy Linear URLs, issue bodies, tokens or other private details into commits, PRs, code or docs in the repo. End the reply with `Tracked: ASK-n (few-word description, new), ASK-m (…, updated)`. When several tickets in the current milestone are independent (disjoint packages/files), work them with parallel subagents; keep coupled ones sequential. Procedure: .claude/issue-tracker.md."}}
JSON
